{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2 Arial;}{\f1\fswiss\fprq2 Calibri;}{\f2\fnil\fcharset0 Segoe UI;}}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs28\b FutaRide Technical Documentation\b0\par\pard\f1\fs18\par Prepared By: OLOWOYO Oluwaseun\par Date: October 9, 2026\par Repository: TheOluwaseunOO/FutaRide\par Live Application: https://futa-ride.vercel.app\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Executive Summary\b0\par\f1\fs18\par FutaRide is a smart campus mobility web application designed for FUTA (Federal University of Technology, Akure). It helps students, riders, drivers, and administrators connect in a structured, role-based transportation system.\par\par The application provides a responsive interface, secure authentication, route protections, role-specific dashboards, and a scalable front-end built with React and TypeScript.\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Repository Information\b0\par\f1\fs18\par Repository Name: FutaRide\par Owner: TheOluwaseunOO\par Repository ID: 1375630138\par Primary Language: TypeScript (97.5%)\par Secondary Language: JavaScript (1.4%)\par Other: 1.1%\par Visibility: Public\par Default Branch: main\par Live App: https://futa-ride.vercel.app\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Technical Stack\b0\par\f1\fs18\par Frontend Framework: React 19\par Language: TypeScript 5.7\par Routing: React Router DOM 7\par Styling: Tailwind CSS v4\par Build Tool: Vite 8\par Backend: Supabase 2\par Code Formatter: oxfmt\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Project Structure\b0\par\f1\fs18\par src/\par - pages/\par - components/\par - context/\par - lib/\par - hooks/\par - assets/\par - tests/\par - App.tsx\par - main.tsx\par - index.css\par public/\par - favicon.png\par - logo.png\par - logo-white.png\par - sw.js\par supabase/\par - config.toml\par - functions/\par package.json\par vite.config.ts\par tsconfig.json\par vercel.json\par AGENTS.md\par CLAUDE.md\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Architecture Overview\b0\par\f1\fs18\par The app boots from index.html into src/main.tsx, wraps the app in BrowserRouter and AuthProvider, and routes users through App.tsx. The route logic directs users to Landing, AuthPage, StudentDashboard, DriverDashboard, or AdminDashboard based on role and URL. Role-based access is enforced through RoleGuard.\par\par Authentication is handled using Supabase Auth and user metadata/profile data is normalized and stored in the application state.\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Key Features\b0\par\f1\fs18\par - Public landing page\par - Rider/student authentication\par - Driver authentication\par - Admin login and dashboard\par - Role-based route protection\par - User profile fetching and session management\par - Online/offline banner\par - Ride cancellation modal\par - Loading skeletons and empty states\par - Service worker for offline support\par\pard\f0\fs24\b User Roles\b0\par\f1\fs18\par Rider/Student: Can access the rider portal and manage ride activities.\par Driver: Can access the driver dashboard and manage active rides.\par Administrator: Can access admin features and system-level controls.\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Installation and Setup\b0\par\f1\fs18\par Prerequisites:\par - Node.js 18+\par - npm or package manager\par - Git\par - Supabase account\par\par Steps:\par 1. Clone the repository\par 2. Run npm install\par 3. Configure environment variables\par 4. Start the development server with npm run dev\par\par Scripts:\par - npm run dev\par - npm run build\par - npm run preview\par - npm run format\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Deployment\b0\par\f1\fs18\par The application is deployed on Vercel. A vercel.json configuration rewrites all non-file routes to index.html for proper SPA routing.\par\par Production build command:\par npm run build\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Styling and UI\b0\par\f1\fs18\par The project uses Tailwind CSS v4 with a custom theme. The design system includes colors such as white, dark gray, and brand orange accent (#E6900E). Typography is set using Inter, Outfit, and JetBrains Mono.\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Authentication and Profiles\b0\par\f1\fs18\par AuthContext exposes user, profile, loading, signUp, signIn, signOut, and fetchProfile methods. It checks the current Supabase session and reloads the user profile as needed. Profiles include fields such as full_name, phone_number, role, vehicle_plate_number, and matric_number.\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Best Practices Used\b0\par\f1\fs18\par - TypeScript strict mode\par - Component-based architecture\par - Context API for global auth state\par - Tailwind CSS utility-first styling\par - Role-based access protection\par - Modular project organization\par - Vite for fast build tooling\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Future Enhancements\b0\par\f1\fs18\par - Add automated tests\par - Improve error handling\par - Add CI/CD workflows\par - Add API documentation\par - Expand ride analytics and notifications\par - Add payment integrations and advanced user features\par\pard\f0\fs24\b Conclusion\b0\par\f1\fs18\par FutaRide is a modern, scalable, and role-based transportation platform for campus mobility. It demonstrates strong frontend architecture, clean component organization, secure authentication patterns, and a production-ready deployment setup.\par\pard\f0\fs18\par End of Documentation\par}\pard\f1\fs16\par\par This file is saved in Microsoft Word-compatible RTF format for easy opening in Word, Google Docs, and other document editors.\par\par The full version is also available in GitHub Markdown here: https://github.com/TheOluwaseunOO/FutaRide/blob/main/DOCUMENTATION.md\par}